up and measured 2026-08-18 (Exp11) — Table VII and Fig. blockchain_cost in
the current manuscript already reflect this. Use instead:

  "Thank you for this important observation. We have addressed this
   directly: the blockchain evaluation now reports measurements from a
   live 3-node Ethereum Clique-PoA consortium (t=2s block period), with
   all three nodes independently peered and mining, rather than a
   single-node testbed. For each finalized epoch we report gas
   consumption (43,829.80 +/- 3.69 gas), serialized transaction payload
   (124 +/- 0 bytes), and confirmation latency (5.877 +/- 0.438 s), mean
   +/- SD over 20 independent epoch submissions. We additionally measured
   cross-node propagation latency -- the time for a newly anchored epoch
   to become visible on the other two nodes -- which averaged 4.3-4.9 ms
   across block intervals of 1, 2, 5, and 15 s, confirming that consensus
   overhead is small relative to the ~5.9 s confirmation latency itself.
   These results and the resulting ledger-growth projection across block
   intervals are reported in the new Blockchain Anchoring Overhead
